@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il08-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-schedule-a1-part-d`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Tests for Schedule A1, Part D. Row IL-08.
--
-- Every expected value is a row of the printed table (lines 4438-4453, quoted in
-- nii-schedule-a1-part-d.l4), turned into months by hand: years x 12 plus the months printed.
-- Each band is tested at its first and its last month of birth, so that a misplaced edge fails.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Tests — Schedule A1, Part D`

-- "עד יוני 1939": 65 years, 780 months.
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 1 `of` 1930 EQUALS 780
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 6 `of` 1939 EQUALS 780
-- July and August 1939: 65 and 4 months, 784 (row IL-05's example).
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 7 `of` 1939 EQUALS 784
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 8 `of` 1939 EQUALS 784
-- September 1939 to April 1940: 65 and 8 months, 788.
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 9 `of` 1939 EQUALS 788
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 4 `of` 1940 EQUALS 788
-- May to December 1940: 66, 792.
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 5 `of` 1940 EQUALS 792
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 12 `of` 1940 EQUALS 792
-- January to August 1941: 66 and 4 months, 796.
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 1 `of` 1941 EQUALS 796
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 8 `of` 1941 EQUALS 796
-- September 1941 to April 1942: 66 and 8 months, 800.
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 9 `of` 1941 EQUALS 800
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 4 `of` 1942 EQUALS 800
-- May 1942 to December 1944: 67, 804.
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 5 `of` 1942 EQUALS 804
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 12 `of` 1944 EQUALS 804
-- January to August 1945: 67 and 4 months, 808.
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 1 `of` 1945 EQUALS 808
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 8 `of` 1945 EQUALS 808
-- September 1945 to April 1946: 67 and 8 months, 812.
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 9 `of` 1945 EQUALS 812
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 4 `of` 1946 EQUALS 812
-- May to December 1946: 68, 816.
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 5 `of` 1946 EQUALS 816
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 12 `of` 1946 EQUALS 816
-- January to August 1947: 68 and 4 months, 820.
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 1 `of` 1947 EQUALS 820
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 8 `of` 1947 EQUALS 820
-- September 1947 to April 1948: 68 and 8 months, 824.
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 9 `of` 1947 EQUALS 824
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 4 `of` 1948 EQUALS 824
-- May to December 1948: 69, 828.
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 5 `of` 1948 EQUALS 828
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 12 `of` 1948 EQUALS 828
-- January to August 1949: 69 and 4 months, 832.
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 1 `of` 1949 EQUALS 832
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 8 `of` 1949 EQUALS 832
-- September 1949 to April 1950: 69 and 8 months, 836.
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 9 `of` 1949 EQUALS 836
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 4 `of` 1950 EQUALS 836
-- May 1950 and after: 70, 840 (the figure row IL-07's tests supply).
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 5 `of` 1950 EQUALS 840
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born in month` 3 `of` 1990 EQUALS 840

-- From a date of birth: only the month and year are read.
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born on` (YMD 1945 8 31) EQUALS 808
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born on` (YMD 1945 9 1) EQUALS 812
-- The day she reaches it: born 15 March 1946, 812 months (67 years and 8 months) on: 15 November 2013.
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the day she reaches the age it fixes for her, for a woman born on` (YMD 1946 3 15) EQUALS YMD 2013 11 15
-- Born 31 January 1949, 832 months (69 years and 4 months): 31 May 2018.
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the day she reaches the age it fixes for her, for a woman born on` (YMD 1949 1 31) EQUALS YMD 2018 5 31
-- Born 30 June 1950: 70 years on, 30 June 2020.
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the day she reaches the age it fixes for her, for a woman born on` (YMD 1950 6 30) EQUALS YMD 2020 6 30
-- Version 0.3.0: the three assertions above land on days that exist, so they do not rest on the
-- clamp of versions 0.1.0 to 0.2.0 and are left at the default reading, values unchanged.

§§ `A day the later month lacks (fork N4, ruled by Meng on 2026-10-08, SHRUG; version 0.3.0)`

-- Each expected value worked from the printed rows before the run. Default: declined by name; the
-- last day of the shorter month and the 1st of the next month asked by name.
-- N4-1 to N4-4 (the tester's D-46): born 31 October 1945, row "ספטמבר 1945 עד אפריל 1946" (line 4446),
-- 67 and 8 months = 67 x 12 + 8 = 812. October 1945 + 67 years = October 2012, + 8 months = June 2013,
-- which has 30 days: no 31 June.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Schedule A1, Part D — the day she reaches the age it fixes for her, for a woman born on` (YMD 1945 10 31) BECAUSE "Part D of Schedule A1 fixes an age in years and months, and does not say which day a woman reaches it where the month she reaches it in lacks her day of birth"
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the day she reaches the age it fixes for her, for a woman born on` (YMD 1945 10 31) `, reading a day the month lacks as` `Part D: the last day of the shorter month` EQUALS YMD 2013 6 30
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the day she reaches the age it fixes for her, for a woman born on` (YMD 1945 10 31) `, reading a day the month lacks as` `Part D: the 1st of the next month` EQUALS YMD 2013 7 1
#ASSERT REFUSED `Schedule A1, Part D — the day she reaches the age it fixes for her, for a woman born on` (YMD 1945 10 31) `, reading a day the month lacks as` `Part D: such a day is declined` BECAUSE "Part D of Schedule A1 fixes an age in years and months, and does not say which day a woman reaches it where the month she reaches it in lacks her day of birth"
-- N4-5 to N4-7 (the tester's D-47): born 29 February 1944, row "מאי 1942 עד דצמבר 1944" (line 4444),
-- 67 = 804 months. February 1944 + 67 years = February 2011, a common year (2011 = 4 x 502 + 3).
#ASSERT REFUSED `Schedule A1, Part D — the day she reaches the age it fixes for her, for a woman born on` (YMD 1944 2 29) BECAUSE "Part D of Schedule A1 fixes an age in years and months, and does not say which day a woman reaches it where the month she reaches it in lacks her day of birth"
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the day she reaches the age it fixes for her, for a woman born on` (YMD 1944 2 29) `, reading a day the month lacks as` `Part D: the last day of the shorter month` EQUALS YMD 2011 2 28
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the day she reaches the age it fixes for her, for a woman born on` (YMD 1944 2 29) `, reading a day the month lacks as` `Part D: the 1st of the next month` EQUALS YMD 2011 3 1
-- N4-8 to N4-10 (the tester's D-48): born 31 July 1945, row "ינואר עד אוגוסט 1945" (line 4445), 67 and
-- 4 months = 808. July 1945 + 67 years = July 2012, + 4 months = November 2012, which has 30 days.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Schedule A1, Part D — the day she reaches the age it fixes for her, for a woman born on` (YMD 1945 7 31) BECAUSE "Part D of Schedule A1 fixes an age in years and months, and does not say which day a woman reaches it where the month she reaches it in lacks her day of birth"
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the day she reaches the age it fixes for her, for a woman born on` (YMD 1945 7 31) `, reading a day the month lacks as` `Part D: the last day of the shorter month` EQUALS YMD 2012 11 30
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the day she reaches the age it fixes for her, for a woman born on` (YMD 1945 7 31) `, reading a day the month lacks as` `Part D: the 1st of the next month` EQUALS YMD 2012 12 1
-- N4-11 to N4-13: a day that exists is the same under all three readings. Born 15 March 1946, 812
-- months (as above): March 2013 + 8 months = 15 November 2013.
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the day she reaches the age it fixes for her, for a woman born on` (YMD 1946 3 15) `, reading a day the month lacks as` `Part D: the last day of the shorter month` EQUALS YMD 2013 11 15
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the day she reaches the age it fixes for her, for a woman born on` (YMD 1946 3 15) `, reading a day the month lacks as` `Part D: the 1st of the next month` EQUALS YMD 2013 11 15
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the day she reaches the age it fixes for her, for a woman born on` (YMD 1946 3 15) `, reading a day the month lacks as` `Part D: such a day is declined` EQUALS YMD 2013 11 15
-- N4-14: born 30 October 1945, 812 months on: June 2013 has a 30th, so the default answers 30 June 2013.
#ASSERT `Schedule A1, Part D — the day she reaches the age it fixes for her, for a woman born on` (YMD 1945 10 30) EQUALS YMD 2013 6 30
